build/
# Your seed space: the reference PDFs and .bib files you drop in. Loom reads it, never writes it,
# and copies what it has not seen into the store below; the entries it reads are committed there.
refs/
# Loom's store of other people's documents, keyed by the work's identifier: fetched or copied,
# never written by you.
digests/storage/**/paper.pdf
digests/storage/**/src/
digests/storage/cache/
# But `digests/storage/**/pages/`, `sections.json` and `copied.json` ARE committed. They are the
# page text an anchor names, which is what lets a coauthor who holds no PDF re-check a
# transcription, and the record of every document ever copied, which is what stops a second copy.
# loom's cache of the last text it saw for every key: one copy of the quilt, rebuilt on demand
last-seen.json
.loom/serve.json
# loom's clone of the document workspace (an Overleaf project), made by `loom sync init`: a repository of its own, never part of this one
.loom/workspace/
# Where each agent last looked, which `loom since` reports from: one marker per agent name, on this machine only
.loom/since/
# What starts loom's MCP server for each agent's app, written by `loom ai init`: it names this machine's loom and this quilt's path, so every machine writes its own
.mcp.json
.codex/config.toml
.gemini/settings.json
.cursor/mcp.json
# LaTeX artifacts a hand compile scatters at the root or in drafting/; loom's own outputs all land under build/
